    "https://pleiades.stoa.org/vocabularies/place-types/province-2"
  ],
  "details": "<p>The place-names of the Hither Province settlements run north to south along the west coast of Messenia.</p>\r\n<p><span style=\"text-decoration: underline; \">Likely geography of the Hither Province:</span>\u00a0<em>(see Bennet 2011 p. 152 and Cosmopoulos 2006 p. 205-6)</em></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>North boundary: either the River Neda or the Kyparissia valley.</li>\r\n<li>South boundary: Cape Akritas, somewhere north of modern Koroni.</li>\r\n<li>West boundary: the coast of Messenia.</li>\r\n<li>East boundary: Mount Aigaleon.</li>\r\n</ul>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "The Hither Province of Mycenaean Pylos, containing nine settlements as recorded in the Linear B tablets.",
